WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.340
Ready to go back to Derry?

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.580
The first trailer for It: Chapter Two has
arrived, and it looks like writer-director

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.300
Andy Muschietti might just pull it off again.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.640
"Hello."

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:18.039
Though most of the clip is devoted to one
scene, there are a few small but telling details

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.140
that you might have missed.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.060
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.500
Meet Mrs. Kersh.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.580
Most of the trailer finds Beverly Marsh returning
to her father's old home.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.060
The new resident seems like a nice enough
old lady, doesn't she?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.770
Meanwhile, Bev is heartened to discover the
old "January embers" poem that Ben wrote for

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.660
her so many decades before.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.080
But the atmosphere in the apartment grows
eerier by the second, especially when Mrs.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.840
Kersh's starts verbally tormenting Beverly:

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.540
"I was always daddy's little girl.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.480
What about you?"

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.580
If you read Stephen King's massive novel It,
you'll remember this moment as one of the

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.280
creepiest scenes in the book.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.480
In the novel, Mrs. Kersh transforms into a
yellow-toothed witch.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.080
The trailer doesn't quite show us what she'll
become in the movie, but we're already covering

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:05.980
our eyes.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:10.560
Here's another detail from the trailer that
really stands out: The Losers Club appears

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.800
to have thinned out.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.600
Although the group still sees young Stanley
Uris and Eddie Kaspbrak in a window reflection,

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:22.170
there are now only five of them standing as
adults: Isaiah Mustafa's Mike Hanlon, Bill

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:27.740
Hader's Richie Tozier, James McAvoy's Bill
Denbrough, Jessica Chastain's Beverly, and

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.500
Jay Ryan's Ben Hanscom.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:34.200
If you read King's novel, you know that Stanley
Uris never makes it back to Derry.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.640
Eddie does join the group for the second battle
against Pennywise, but his fate isn't as fortunate

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.640
as the rest.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.280
However, in the book, Eddie's death takes
place late in the action.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.440
Perhaps the glimpse we see in the trailer
is from the tail end of the film, after The

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.020
Losers Club's last stand with Pennywise.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.380
Or maybe Eddie just dashed off to the pharmacy
to pick up a new inhaler?

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.660
Time will tell.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.760
The settings in the trailer for It: Chapter
Two are entirely familiar.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.280
Evidently, Derry hasn't put much money for
renovations over the last 27 years.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:09.300
One location seems to carry some major significance,
though, and we're not talking about the sewer,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.720
although there's bound to be plenty of action
down there, too.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.300
No, we're talking about this grassy hill.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:19.060
As you may recall, it looks like the exact
same spot the kids visited to make their blood

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.520
oath in the first film.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:29.700
"S-swear if it isn't dead, if it ever comes
back, we'll come back, too."

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.560
It's also the same spot that both Stan and
Eddie seemed to confirm their fates by leaving

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.320
the group first, in the same order they die
in.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.000
Surprisingly, the exit order doesn't seem
to be repeated in this trailer.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.740
If you look closely, it's Richie Tozier who
trails the group instead of Eddie.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.560
You may want to avoid Chinese food for a while.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.900
As we see in the trailer, the Losers Club
heads over to the Jade of the Orient restaurant

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.200
for a reunion meal, just like in the book.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.980
"This meeting of the Losers Club has officially
begun."

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:02.940
The trailer only shows their arrival, but
King fans, and anyone who saw the 1990 TV

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:06.780
miniseries, will remember just how unappetizing
things get.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:11.340
So many unspeakable horrors can fit into those
teeny tiny fortune cookies.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.380
Guess we'll have to wait and see what ghastly
surprises IT has in store.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.720
The trailer also calls back to a fixture of
King's book and the 2017 adaptation: the giant

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.240
statue of Paul Bunyan in the town park.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:27.560
It's there in the first film, when the Losers
gather together to discuss Pennywise.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.560
In the book, it becomes animated and taunts
Richie.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.480
It: Chapter Two brings the statue back into
Richie's life, but we don't see it in motion

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.480
just yet.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:41.340
Instead, Pennywise is seen floating above
it, suspended by an inverted pyramid of balloons.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:46.180
Even so, the Paul Bunyan statue's importance
clearly hasn't been overlooked by the director.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:51.300
King fans also know that the statue really
exists in Bangor, Maine, and freaks out the

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.000
locals on a regular basis.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.580
The first chapter of It thankfully didn't
deal with the Ritual of Chüd or Maturin the

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.460
celestial turtle, but fans know that these
otherworldly concepts will make it into Chapter

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:02.460
Two.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:07.060
The trailer appears to confirm it: The Losers
hit the sewers to track down Pennywise and

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.560
come upon a giant spiky object.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.780
We see the gang holding hands and looking
up at the ceiling, or, more likely, something

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:15.160
beyond the ceiling.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:19.720
We never get a glimpse of the creature in
the trailer, but we imagine, we hope, it'll

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.700
be more frightening than that thing we saw
in the miniseries.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:27.480
We know Muschietti plans to bring the inter-dimensional
element of It to the big screen in Chapter

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.380
Two, and this is our first look at how that
might happen.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:31.840
Scared?

